From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muse <muse@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:54:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios launcher: Simplified Chinese on a Chinese device

The single-game launcher (dm/ios) hardcodes English and its project.yml
declares no CFBundleLocalizations, so a device set to Chinese shows
English everywhere, unlike the shell (patches 0055/0056). DmL10n in
LauncherSettings.swift returns the Simplified Chinese of a text when
the preferred language is Chinese and the text itself otherwise. The
setting rows take the Mac launcher's translations (frontend/l10n
launch.* and ios.setting.*), the screen's own texts are translated
with them, and project.yml declares en and zh-Hans.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: the single-game launcher hardcodes English and declares no localizations, so a Chinese device shows English
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#418

---
 dm/ios/Sources/GameMenu.swift         |  12 +--
 dm/ios/Sources/Launcher.swift         |  46 ++++++------
 dm/ios/Sources/LauncherRow.swift      |  10 +--
 dm/ios/Sources/LauncherSettings.swift | 103 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dm/ios/project.yml                    |   1 +
 5 files changed, 138 insertions(+), 34 deletions(-)

